Tex Haeuser wrote:

> Hi--I'm a Val with St:25 Dx:18 Co:18 In:8 Wi:16 Ch:11 HP: 155 Pw:70
> AC:-7 Exp:17.  I've got the Orb of Fate with 3 charges.  I'm in the
> Castle and I foolishly plugged all the trap doors down to the next
> level with boulders. Digging through the boulders didn't work, so I
> tried to level transport by applying and invoking the Orb of Fate,
> from the Castle and from another level, but it's either
> hallucinating, confusing, or ignoring me.  Is that because my
> intelligence is too low?  Is there any other way I can get to the
> next level?

The Orb's charges count towards you (a)pplying it, and function like any
ordinary glass orb: you may look for an object or something like that.
Recharging the Orb would give it more "scrying" charges. Your
intelligence is way too low for you to use it effectively to scry.

What you want is to #invoke the Orb, to levelport. This should work no
matter your intelligence. The only thing that matters here is that you
cannot use it too often. If you use it too soon after having used it
earlier, the Orb will "ignore" you, and another 100 turns are added
before you may use it successfully.

> I should also mention that I had already used the Castle's wand of
> wishing on things like gauntlets and speed boots, blowing it up on a
> re-charge (and why does that happen?--I thought I'd let it "cool off"
> enough).  Perhaps it's surprising I've gotten this far.

You can recharge wands of wishing and magic markers only once. At the
second recharging attempt, they will blow up. Wands don't need to cool
off, whatever you mean by that.

Wands other than wishing may be recharged more than once, but the more
you have charged them before, the greater the chance they will blow up.
I believe wands that have been recharged seven times will always blow up
when you attempt to charge them again.

